From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:07:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: require a checked tweeter high-pass in front of
 SP RX

SP RX's own high-pass is a single ~80 Hz filter on all channels, so a
stream that bypasses a userspace crossover reaches the tweeters full
band. As on Windows, high-pass the tweeters in the DSP with an MSIIR
ahead of SP, and have the kernel check the graph:

- at the first setup after topology load: one SP RX and one SP VI, and
  SP RX in the chain MFC -> [MSIIR ->] SP -> MFC -> ... -> the WSA RX0
  codec DMA sink, one link each, with single input ports from the MSIIR
  on so no other graph can join downstream of the filter;
- nothing after SP remixes or amplifies: the MFCs next to SP carry no
  cfg blob, and where SP or the high-pass is required only data
  logging may follow the second one;
- with tweeters listed, the MSIIR carries exactly the qualified filter,
  a 4th order Linkwitz-Riley high-pass at 1.5 kHz, 48 kHz, on every
  channel type but the woofers' FL and FR; each prepare checks the rate
  and that every listed speaker's channel type is filtered;
- blobs that would change the SP modes, R0/T0 or test modes are
  refused, and raw cfg blobs may only address their own module.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
